<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman rates IMI &quot;outperform&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman rates IMI &quot;outperform&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said on Tuesday it was initiating coverage of British engineering firm IMI Plc with an &quot;outperform&quot; rating.</p>
<p>Lehman said its 1997 price target for the company was 440p, while its 1998 target was 500p.  </p>
<p>&quot;Most of the sectors in which IMI competes are generally unconsolidated, typically with the top few global layers holding only a relatively small part of the market, the rest of the market being made up of small local or regional players,&quot; Lehman analyst Charles Armitage said in a research note.</p>
<p>&quot;This gives IMI the opportunity to expand through acquisition and realising the benefits of scale.&quot;</p>
<p>IMI shares were 1/2p higher at 375 by 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
